==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɑːft|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|hæft|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*haftiją}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[handle]] of a [[tool]] or [[weapon]].
#* Dryden
#*: This brandish'd dagger / I'll bury to the '''haft''' in her fair breast.

=====Synonyms=====
* [[hilt]] (''sword handle'')
* [[stale]], [[stail]], [[stele]], [[steal]] (''axe handle'')

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|handle}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|heft|n}}, {{t+|nl|greep|m}}, {{t+|nl|handvat|n}}, {{t|nl|handgreep|m}}
* Georgian: {{t+|ka|ვადა}}
* Hebrew: {{t+|he|קת|f}} (kat), {{t+|he|ידית|f}} (yadít)
* Italian: {{t+|it|elsa|f}}, {{t|it|coccia|f}}, {{t+|it|impugnatura|f}}, {{t|it|guardamano|m}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Russian: {{t+|ru|ру́чка|f}}, {{t+|ru|рукоя́тка|f}}, {{t+|ru|черено́к|m}}
* Scottish Gaelic: {{t|gd|lurgann|f}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|empuñadura|m}}, {{t|es|asidero|m}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To fit a handle to a tool or weapon.

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|fit a handle}}
* Dutch: {{t|nl|er een handvat aanzetten}}, {{t+|nl|vatten}}
{{trans-mid}}
